PURPOSE
H84 and H96 suggest a more general developmental cognition motif:

maintain:
multiple hypotheses;

let them:
predict,
disagree,
earn fit,
go dormant,
and
be challenged;

spend:
real evidence
only when:
its information value exceeds cost.

The first H97 formulation failed because:
raw surprise triggered too many experiments
and
hard pruning destroyed recurring causal structure.

H97 rebuilds the experiment around:
- dormant hypothesis retention;
- persistent regime-change suspicion;
- information-gain-gated challenge;
- explicit model-fit failure state.

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- implement a production causal-discovery engine;
- prove fixed hypothesis libraries are sufficient;
- freeze the challenge-cost threshold;
- establish final model-birth rules;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

